    "title": "pandas.errors.ValueLabelTypeMismatch — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1663.g6eba694f5d documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.errors.ValueLabelTypeMismatch#\n\n- exception pandas.errors.ValueLabelTypeMismatch[source]#\n- Warning raised by to_stata on a category column that contains non-string values. When exporting data to Stata format using the to_stata method, category columns must have string values as labels. If a category column contains non-string values (e.g., integers, floats, or other types), this warning is raised to indicate that the Stata file may not correctly represent the data. See also \n  - `DataFrame.to_stata`\n  - Export DataFrame object to Stata dta format.\n  - `Series.cat`\n  - Accessor for categorical properties of the Series values.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"categories\": pd.Series([\"a\", 2], dtype=\"category\")}) >>> df.to_stata(\"test\")",
